		<readme type="inline"><![CDATA[
Theme Lab 1.0.2

After installation:
1. Open Administration Center > Configuration > Theme Lab.
2. Run Environment Check.
3. Create a new Workspace, or import a Theme Lab workspace/theme.
4. Work through the Studios and use the live preview while designing.
5. Open Review to check the completed design.
6. Open Publish to build the finished SMF theme package.

Uninstalling always removes Theme Lab files, hooks, and runtime settings. In SMF Package Manager, leave the database-removal option unchecked to preserve saved Workspaces for a later reinstall. Enable database removal only when you deliberately want to delete Theme Lab Workspace data. Published themes are independent and are not removed with Theme Lab.
        ]]></readme>

